<node id="CORNWALL">
  <data key="d0">CORNWALL</data>
  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">A location in Cornwall, described as a place with cliffs, sea, and natural beauty. It is mentioned as a place where the narrator and others strolled and reflected on their experiences.&lt;SEP&gt;A location in England with historical and cultural significance. The storm is described as being particularly severe in this area, and it is associated with the characters' holiday plans.&lt;SEP&gt;A region in England known for its coastal landscapes and rich cultural heritage. It is mentioned as the setting where the man and his wife live, and it is associated with local legends and traditions. The region is also linked to the lighthouse and the story of the Emperor's involvement in its lighting. Cornwall is depicted as a place of deep historical and emotional significance.&lt;SEP&gt;A region in England known for its rugged coastline and historical significance in maritime activities. The text highlights the dangers of the coast, including frequent shipwrecks and the role of the coast-guard in saving lives.&lt;SEP&gt;Cornwall is a coastal region in England known for its rugged landscapes and cultural significance. It is described as a place of adventure and historical importance, particularly associated with figures like King Arthur and Jack the Giantkiller. Key attributes include its natural beauty, historical myths, and cultural identity. It has a relationship with the author, who wishes to explore it. Historically, Cornwall is linked to legends of bravery and justice. Notable events include the author's desire to visit Land's End and the mention of the Cornish people's values.&lt;SEP&gt;Cornwall is a county in the southwest of England, known for its rugged coastline, historic sites, and cultural heritage. The text describes a journey through Cornwall, emphasizing its natural beauty and the atmosphere of the region. Cornwall is a significant location in the narrative, representing a landscape that inspired the legends of King Arthur.&lt;SEP&gt;Cornwall is a location in England, noted for its unique landscape and the grey cows that are characteristic of the region. It plays a significant role in the narrative, as the setting where the events take place and where the natural beauty and cultural elements are highlighted.&lt;SEP&gt;Cornwall is a region in England known for its rugged coastline and scenic landscapes. It is mentioned as the location of Mullion Cove, contributing to the natural and cultural context of the narrative. The region is associated with the presence of sea-caves and the unique environment that attracts visitors.&lt;SEP&gt;Cornwall is the primary location of the journey described in the text. It is a region in England known for its coastal landscapes, historical sites, and cultural significance. The journey through Cornwall is the central theme of the book.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59fd7b8af627bbbd404acb5ac88aef98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6196f7575ff952a3f5db2b2d296af03f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c13d92c83041a8623279efdde8af1707&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc03c3ac54e7909422a954e2a66def93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfb65c6e4369170c3277959468b587be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dca5f3a8de43d3e2bc3bc88b3703f62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d3c8ddcaba7527f7fcbf3bec3621635&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad3c1e9f9f896847e83e5929f169df65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaa5de23ba6f27901db4cc60fd6df0ae</data>
