<node id="ST. MICHAEL'S MOUNT">
  <data key="d0">ST. MICHAEL'S MOUNT</data>
  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">A historic and legendary site in Mount's Bay, resembling Mont St. Michel in Normandy. It is associated with numerous legends, including those of the giant Cormoran and the saint St. Keyne. The Mount is a central point of interest in the narrative and is linked to many historical figures and events.&lt;SEP&gt;A historic and unique location in England, characterized by a medieval fortress and modern residence. It is described as a place where a fishing village coexists with a hilltop settlement, and it serves as a home to the St. Aubyns. The location is notable for its natural beauty, historical artifacts, and the challenges of living there, such as the difficulty of accessing the top of the rock. It is central to the narrative and represents a blend of history and daily life.&lt;SEP&gt;St. Michael's Mount is a notable landmark in Cornwall. It is referenced as an illustration in the book, indicating its significance in the region's geography and culture.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6196f7575ff952a3f5db2b2d296af03f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-369d72e297f786886a6ee02d55512e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-744360fec46b02217eb1d4d9f455cb8a</data>
  <data key="d4">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 16}]</data>
</node>
<node id="FALMOUTH">
  <data key="d0">FALMOUTH</data>
  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">A location in Cornwall, England, from which some of the tourists arrive. It is mentioned as a possible origin for the pic-nic parties that come to Kynance Sands.&lt;SEP&gt;A location in Cornwall, England, where the travelers initially stayed before moving on to the Lizard. The entity is significant as it was the starting point of their journey. Key attributes include being a quiet and peaceful place with a sea view. The entity is connected to the narrator and the friend through their stay there. It has historical significance as a traditional resting place.&lt;SEP&gt;Falmouth is a coastal town in Cornwall, England, known for its harbor and scenic beauty. It is mentioned as a destination on the journey, and the Green Bank Hotel is referenced as a place to stay. Falmouth is significant for its natural beauty and historical relevance.&lt;SEP&gt;Falmouth is a coastal town in Cornwall, serving as a starting point for the journey described in the text. It is an important location in the narrative, representing a transition from urban to rural and natural environments. Falmouth is also a port city, historically significant for maritime activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Falmouth is a town in Cornwall, mentioned in the text. It is a coastal area known for its harbor and historical significance. The town is part of the journey described in the book.&lt;SEP&gt;Falmouth is a town mentioned in the text. It is referenced as a place from which pic-nic parties often come to Mullion. It is connected to the horse that Charles uses for transportation.&lt;SEP&gt;Falmouth is a town or city mentioned in the text, where Charles is expected to return. It is referenced as a destination for Charles and his carriage, suggesting it is a significant location in the narrative.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6196f7575ff952a3f5db2b2d296af03f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f15d171fef48d074f3c095117c010dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-743cd293533b6212903371567d44500f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85b0c1bb6db9932af72e242802e01101&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e785b114eb81de96943779a460bab162&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ee024234b415f45ea0006087720bb09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c527f463c6b54a8cb919a64d12423b24</data>
