<node id="RISTORMEL">
  <data key="d0">RISTORMEL</data>
  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">A location in Cornwall, England, which is described as an ancient castle. It is mentioned as part of the scenic railway journey through the region. The area is noted for its historical significance and is part of the route taken by the travelers.&lt;SEP&gt;Ristormel is an old castle in Cornwall, England, noted among the three castles of the region. It is mentioned as a site of historical interest, and the travelers are shown its remains. Ristormel is significant for its historical and cultural value.&lt;SEP&gt;Ristormel is one of the ancient castles of Cornwall, mentioned as a fleeting vision during the journey. It represents the historical and cultural heritage of the region, often associated with medieval legends and the Arthurian lore. Its presence in the text highlights the rich history of Cornwall and its connection to the Arthurian legend.</data>
