  <data key="d0">ST. MAWES CASTLE</data>
  <data key="d1">ARTWORK</data>
  <data key="d2">St. Mawes Castle is a historic castle located in Falmouth Bay, Cornwall. It is mentioned as an illustration in the text and is part of the landscape the travelers observe. The castle is a notable landmark and adds to the historical context of the journey.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f15d171fef48d074f3c095117c010dc</data>
</node>
<node id="OLD GENTLEMAN">
  <data key="d0">OLD GENTLEMAN</data>
  <data key="d1">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d2">An elderly man who is part of the group at Kynance Sands. He is described as having a thoughtful and prudent nature, and he shares a conversation with the narrator about the behavior of young people. He is also recognized by the narrator for his voice, which reminds them of Frederick Denison Maurice.&lt;SEP&gt;An old gentleman is a character in the text who interacts with the travelers. He provides advice about traveling in Cornwall and shares his experiences. His role is to offer guidance and reflect on local customs and attitudes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f15d171fef48d074f3c095117c010dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c527f463c6b54a8cb919a64d12423b24</data>
