</node>
<node id="NARRATOR">
  <data key="d0">NARRATOR</data>
  <data key="d1">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d2">A person who is part of the group traveling and is described as one of the 'unprotected females.' The entity plays a central role in the narrative, experiencing the journey and interacting with other characters. Key attributes include being a traveler and having a sense of adventure. The entity is connected to other characters like Charles and the friend who met them in Falmouth. There is no specific historical or cultural relevance mentioned for this entity.&lt;SEP&gt;A person who is part of the group visiting Kynance Sands. They are described as being active and brave, but also cautious. They are involved in conversations with the old gentleman and are part of the group that experiences the rising tide.&lt;SEP&gt;A person who is reflecting on their experiences during a journey in Cornwall. They are observing the natural surroundings and contemplating the contrast between human life and the eternal powers of nature. Their thoughts include reflections on death, impermanence, and the significance of solitude.&lt;SEP&gt;An individual who narrates the events of the day, describing their experiences and observations at the Land's End. The narrator interacts with various characters, including the fisher wife and the coastguard, and reflects on the natural beauty and cultural significance of the location. Their perspective shapes the narrative and provides insight into the emotional and intellectual responses to the environment.&lt;SEP&gt;The narrator is an individual who is traveling with Charles and is dependent on his guidance. She is described as being in her later years and experiencing difficulty walking on a narrow path. Her experience highlights the importance of Charles's support and care.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59fd7b8af627bbbd404acb5ac88aef98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85b0c1bb6db9932af72e242802e01101&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5e39286406a99236327034e4840f578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ee024234b415f45ea0006087720bb09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c527f463c6b54a8cb919a64d12423b24</data>
  <data key="d4">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 20}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 42}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 44}]</data>
</node>
<node id="FRIEND">
  <data key="d0">FRIEND</data>
  <data key="d1">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d2">A person mentioned as a friend in Cornwall, whom the group wishes to visit. This indicates a personal connection and a potential point of interaction during their stay.&lt;SEP&gt;A person who met the travelers in Falmouth and provided practical assistance. This entity is significant as they helped secure lodgings and advised the travelers about the Lizard. Key attributes include being a helpful and resourceful individual. The entity is connected to the narrator and the Lizard through their actions. No specific historical or cultural relevance is mentioned for this entity.</data>
