<node id="LIZARD">
  <data key="d0">LIZARD</data>
  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">A location in Cornwall known for its lighthouse, the Lizard Lights. These lights are crucial for guiding ships through dark nights and are described as being visible from far out at sea. The area is also associated with historical shipwrecks and the work of the coast-guard.&lt;SEP&gt;A location in Cornwall, England, known for its scenic beauty and as a destination for sightseers. The entity is significant as it is the main destination of the travelers' journey. Key attributes include being a place of natural beauty and a tourist attraction. The entity is connected to the narrator and the friend through their travel plans. It has historical significance as a well-known landmark in the region.&lt;SEP&gt;A location in England known for its coastal landscape and storms. It is described as being subjected to a severe storm that significantly impacts the characters' stay.&lt;SEP&gt;A location known for its scenic beauty and coastal features. It is described as a high plain with a sparkling sea beyond it, and it includes the Lizard Lights, a significant structure in the area. This place is central to the narrative, where the characters explore and experience nature.&lt;SEP&gt;A nearby town or region associated with the village of Cadgwith. It is mentioned in the context of the parson and his wife, who are described as kind and take care of the invalids in the area. The Lizard is also referenced in relation to the local customs and the lifestyle of the people living in the coastal regions of Cornwall.&lt;SEP&gt;A place in Cornwall noted for its longevity, as evidenced by the records of elderly residents. The Lizard is mentioned in relation to the rector and the community gathering at the rectory tea. It is a significant location within the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Lizard is a geographical feature mentioned in the text. It is described as being near the village of Mullion and is noted for its distinct climate. The Lizard is referenced in relation to the travelers' journey across the downs.&lt;SEP&gt;Lizard is a location in Cornwall where the narrative takes place. It is mentioned as a place with frequent rain and storms, and it is associated with the harvest festival. The location plays a central role in the setting of the story and influences the activities and experiences of the characters.&lt;SEP&gt;Lizard is a town in Cornwall, known for its coastal scenery and the presence of serpentine rock. It is mentioned as a destination in the narrative, where the characters plan to visit shops selling items made from the local stone.&lt;SEP&gt;The Lizard is a headland in Cornwall, described as a place of beauty and tranquility. It is a significant location where the narrator and their companions stayed during their visit. The Lizard is associated with the Lizard Lights and the surrounding natural landscape. It plays a central role in the narrative as a destination for exploration and reflection.&lt;SEP&gt;The Lizard is a headland in Cornwall, known for its rugged coastline and natural beauty. It is a prominent geographical feature in the text, symbolizing the wild and untamed aspects of the Cornish landscape. The Lizard is often associated with dramatic cliffs and unique ecosystems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Lizard is a location mentioned in the text, which is a place where the group stays. It is described as a dot on a map initially but becomes significant to the group due to their experiences there. The Lizard is also the starting point of their journey and is associated with the handmaid Esther.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cfb65c6e4369170c3277959468b587be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-743cd293533b6212903371567d44500f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85b0c1bb6db9932af72e242802e01101&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e302b5e22b09ab16666a0e39faaadeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a11868bbedb00db5ad94f79da20acdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94e0080d8e548382ec3fd09c122e9b19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3755e64526057a08de86199d3391703&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d3c8ddcaba7527f7fcbf3bec3621635&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e785b114eb81de96943779a460bab162&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-445ffbc070c2c6aec738b62a5960af9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9baf49d70e5cdf906cbc1334a05b60e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cff43d4c0b87d4d234e1ded07f8597b</data>
