<node id="CHARLES">
  <data key="d0">CHARLES</data>
  <data key="d1">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d2">A character who is described as faithful and experienced. He is involved in the decision to go boating and provides reassurance about the safety of the trip. His role highlights his reliability and knowledge of the local area.&lt;SEP&gt;A character who is mentioned in the text. He is associated with the idea that Monday is a popular day for excursions, which influences the characters' perspective on the storm.&lt;SEP&gt;A male individual mentioned in the context of a journey with the narrator. He is described as being sensitive to the environment and making decisions to ensure a peaceful experience for the group. His actions suggest a thoughtful and considerate nature.&lt;SEP&gt;A man named Charles who accompanied the travelers. He was present during their visit to Mary Mundy's cottage and participated in the conversation. His role seems to be that of a companion or guide, and he appears to have a good rapport with the locals.&lt;SEP&gt;A person involved in the journey, described as someone who advised the narrator and others to take a guide. He is associated with the carriage and appears to be a driver or companion during the trip.&lt;SEP&gt;A person named Charles who acts as a guide or companion during the journey. He is described as 'patient' and 'ever-watchful,' and he makes decisions about where to go next. His role includes directing the group to places like Poltesco and Cadgwith, and he is responsible for ensuring that the travelers see as much as possible.&lt;SEP&gt;A person who accompanied the narrator on their journey and provided guidance. He is described as faithful and knowledgeable about the local area. Charles plays a key role in helping the group navigate and understand the region's history and landmarks.&lt;SEP&gt;A person who accompanies the narrator on their journey. He is described as kind, helpful, and responsible for transporting them. His role is central to the travel arrangements and interactions.&lt;SEP&gt;A person who is described as a kind and faithful driver. He is responsible for transporting the travelers and is mentioned as being willing to wait for them even after they leave. His loyalty and reliability are emphasized in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;A person who is part of the group exploring the Lizard area. He is described as being in the bow of the boat and referred to as a 'Knight of the Round Table in humble life.' He plays a supportive role in the journey.&lt;SEP&gt;A person who served as the driver for the travelers. This entity is significant as they provided reliable transportation and developed a friendly relationship with the travelers. Key attributes include being a teetotaller and a professional driver. The entity is connected to the narrator and the friend through their service. There is no specific historical or cultural relevance mentioned for this entity.&lt;SEP&gt;An individual who appears to be familiar with the area and provides information about Cadgwith. He is described as someone who considers the village a nice place to winter in, though he notes that it can be a bit dull. His perspective offers insight into the local lifestyle and the perception of the village by residents.&lt;SEP&gt;Charles is a character in the narrative who is familiar with the local geography and culture. He provides commentary on the landscape and points out features like serpentine rock. His role is to guide and inform the narrator about the area.&lt;SEP&gt;Charles is a character in the narrative who plays a central role in making decisions for the group. He is described as thoughtful and willing to adjust plans to accommodate the group's desires. His actions influence the group's itinerary and their ability to visit the sea-caves. He is also shown to be pleased with the changes made to the schedule.&lt;SEP&gt;Charles is a character in the text who acts as a guide and helper to the narrator. He is described as a 'faithful' and 'honest man' who shows care and concern for the narrator's safety. He is also a driver who provides transportation and assistance during their journey. His role is significant as he helps the narrator navigate difficult terrain and ensures their comfort.&lt;SEP&gt;Charles is a character in the text, described as a driver who interacts with the narrator and the two girls. He shares personal stories about his past, including the loss of his wife and child. Charles is portrayed as a kind and thoughtful individual, showing concern for his passengers and the environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Charles is a character who appears in the narrative, bringing a party to the Lizard. He is described as soaked but smiling, showing a sense of camaraderie and concern for the ladies. He plays a role in the social dynamics of the group. His actions suggest he is a friend or acquaintance of the main characters.&lt;SEP&gt;Charles is a character who appears to be a reliable and helpful individual. He is described as punctual and responsible, ensuring that the travelers' needs are met. He is associated with a horse and has a close relationship with Mary Mundy. His role is to assist the travelers and manage their accommodations.&lt;SEP&gt;Charles is a character who assists the narrator during their exploration of the cave. He is described as faithful and helpful, offering guidance and support. His actions contribute to the safety and success of the journey through the cave. He is also mentioned as being thoughtful and considerate towards the narrator.&lt;SEP&gt;Charles is a character who provides transportation and assistance to the group. He is described as a kind and reliable individual who ensures the well-being of the horse and promises to return. His actions and words reflect his role as a supportive figure in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Charles is a person who is described as the driver of the carriage. He plays a key role in the journey by offering to take the characters wherever they want to go. His presence and willingness to help indicate his importance in facilitating the characters' travel plans.&lt;SEP&gt;Charles is a thoughtful character who offers to prepare the carriage for the travelers. He is described as being considerate and helpful, ensuring the group knows the way to the farm-yard. His actions reflect a sense of responsibility and care towards the ladies he is accompanying.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ca4427317d91b282aad105e4c1fcb34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfb65c6e4369170c3277959468b587be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-743cd293533b6212903371567d44500f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-369d72e297f786886a6ee02d55512e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85b0c1bb6db9932af72e242802e01101&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd2b50b24a25833ce136611502f99de5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d113b2b3dce6fe310bc06ea08b364cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3755e64526057a08de86199d3391703&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad3c1e9f9f896847e83e5929f169df65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fb3571cbea81efe6dfda2aa2199fdbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-445ffbc070c2c6aec738b62a5960af9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-000278539400b09a416764f3bc60efe5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cff43d4c0b87d4d234e1ded07f8597b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01da0d7fe4c0b05440c961a17b63f8b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-436157d1f1611fd4639ef4c3e3e77cf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59fd7b8af627bbbd404acb5ac88aef98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c13d92c83041a8623279efdde8af1707&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94e0080d8e548382ec3fd09c122e9b19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d3c8ddcaba7527f7fcbf3bec3621635&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e785b114eb81de96943779a460bab162&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ee024234b415f45ea0006087720bb09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9baf49d70e5cdf906cbc1334a05b60e0</data>
