<node id="CONSTANTINE">
  <data key="d0">CONSTANTINE</data>
  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">A location in Cornwall, England, that the travelers visited after Falmouth. The entity is significant as it is a small village with granite quarries. Key attributes include being a quiet and picturesque place. The entity is connected to the narrator and Charles through their journey. It has historical significance as a site with granite quarries.&lt;SEP&gt;Constantine is another village in Cornwall, noted for its granite quarries. Like Mabe, it contributes to the region's geological and industrial identity. The presence of these quarries highlights the significance of granite in the local landscape and economy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-743cd293533b6212903371567d44500f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85b0c1bb6db9932af72e242802e01101</data>
</node>
<node id="MABE">
  <data key="d0">MABE</data>
  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">A location in Cornwall, England, that the travelers visited after Falmouth. The entity is significant as it is a small village with granite quarries. Key attributes include being a quiet and picturesque place. The entity is connected to the narrator and Charles through their journey. It has historical significance as a site with granite quarries.&lt;SEP&gt;Mabe is a village in Cornwall, known for its granite quarries. It is part of the landscape described in the text, contributing to the natural beauty and geological features of the region. Mabe is associated with the granite industry, which plays a role in the local economy and environment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-743cd293533b6212903371567d44500f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85b0c1bb6db9932af72e242802e01101</data>
