<node id="TRELOWARREN">
  <data key="d0">TRELOWARREN</data>
  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">Trelowarren is a woodland area in Cornwall, home to large trees and a variety of plant life. It is described as a beautiful and serene location, offering a contrast to the more open and barren landscapes of the region. Trelowarren is also associated with the Vyvyan family, highlighting its historical and cultural significance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-743cd293533b6212903371567d44500f</data>
</node>
<node id="HELSTONE">
  <data key="d0">HELSTONE</data>
  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">A location in Cornwall where the travelers arrive after their journey. It is described as a small town with a narrow street that is thronged with beasts and men on market day. The town is significant as it is the destination of the travelers and is known for its sober and civil residents. It is associated with Cornish culture and is a place of rest and food for the travelers.&lt;SEP&gt;A location in Cornwall, England, mentioned as another possible origin for the pic-nic parties that visit Kynance Sands.&lt;SEP&gt;A town or village in Cornwall, mentioned as a place the travelers visited. It is associated with the Loe Pool and other local landmarks. Helstone serves as a backdrop for the narrative and is part of the broader Cornish landscape that is rich in history and legend.&lt;SEP&gt;Helstone is a location mentioned in the text where the group wishes to stay for a while. It is part of their planned route from the Lizard to Penzance and is associated with their desire to meet a friend.&lt;SEP&gt;Helstone is a location mentioned in the text. It is where Mary Mundy is said to have gone for marketing. The travelers are concerned about her absence and whether she will return in time for tea.&lt;SEP&gt;Helstone is a town in Cornwall that serves as an alternative route during the journey. It is mentioned as a regular stop along the way, indicating its importance in the local transportation network. Helstone is less emphasized in the text compared to other locations but still holds relevance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc03c3ac54e7909422a954e2a66def93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-743cd293533b6212903371567d44500f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9527d086956d05f8cfb5def3a68555e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94e0080d8e548382ec3fd09c122e9b19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e785b114eb81de96943779a460bab162&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c527f463c6b54a8cb919a64d12423b24</data>
