<node id="POLTESCO">
  <data key="d0">POLTESCO</data>
  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">A location in Cornwall known for its serpentine works, which are a significant part of the local economy. It is described as having a 'monotonous hum of machinery' and a 'trout-stream.' The place is connected to the 'wooden bridge' and the 'anglers,' and it reflects the industrial and natural aspects of the region.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-436157d1f1611fd4639ef4c3e3e77cf8</data>
</node>
<node id="CRINGO">
  <data key="d0">CRINGO</data>
  <data key="d1">PLANT</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of plant found along the Cornish coast, described as 'grey-green cringo' or 'sea-holly.' It is abundant in the area and is mentioned in the context of the group collecting flowers and plants. This plant contributes to the natural beauty of the region and is part of the local flora.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-436157d1f1611fd4639ef4c3e3e77cf8</data>
