<node id="ROCKS">
  <data key="d0">ROCKS</data>
  <data key="d1">NATURAL_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of rock formation that surrounds the area, creating dangerous conditions for swimmers. These rocks are described as 'innumerable' and are part of the natural hazards of the Cornish coast. They are associated with 'eddies of boiling white water' and represent the perilous nature of the environment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-436157d1f1611fd4639ef4c3e3e77cf8</data>
</node>
<node id="SEA">
  <data key="d0">SEA</data>
  <data key="d1">NATURAL_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">A body of water that is part of the Cornish coast, described as having 'eddies of boiling white water.' It is a dangerous place for swimmers and is associated with the 'cave' and 'floor.' The sea is a central element of the journey and represents both beauty and danger.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-436157d1f1611fd4639ef4c3e3e77cf8</data>
