<node id="RUAN MINOR">
  <data key="d0">RUAN MINOR</data>
  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">A location in Cornwall that is described as having 'a pretty little valley' and a 'trout-stream.' It is associated with the 'wooden bridge' and the 'anglers,' and it reflects the natural and industrial aspects of the region. The place is part of the journey and is connected to the 'serpentine works' in Poltesco.&lt;SEP&gt;An art exhibition that is mentioned in the text. It is described as not being overwhelmingly attractive to the narrator, who had already seen many galleries and museums. However, the exhibition is still significant as it is the subject of the narrator's comment about preferring nature to art.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-445ffbc070c2c6aec738b62a5960af9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-436157d1f1611fd4639ef4c3e3e77cf8</data>
</node>
