  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">The Old Inn is a place where the travelers stop and are welcomed by Mary Mundy. It serves as a resting point and is described as a neat little parlour at the back of the inn. The inn is important in the narrative as it provides shelter and hospitality to the travelers.</data>
