  <data key="d1">ANIMAL</data>
  <data key="d2">Cows are animals mentioned in the narrative, grazing in a field. They are part of the rural landscape and contribute to the setting of the story. Their presence adds to the atmosphere and the sense of normalcy in the environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Cows are described as sleek, calm creatures with Juno-eyed features and soft skin. They are associated with the Cornish landscape and are noted for their color, which harmonizes with the surroundings. The cows are linked to the production of high-quality butter and cream, which are served at Mary Mundy's home.</data>
