<node id="JOHN">
  <data key="d0">JOHN</data>
  <data key="d1">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d2">John is a character in the narrative who speaks about self-control and his personal habits regarding alcohol. He is described as an honest fisherman with a strong sense of self-discipline. John's role in the story is to provide insight into the theme of self-control and to guide the ladies to Kynance Cove. He is also associated with the concept of self-restraint and is seen as a wise and responsible individual.&lt;SEP&gt;John is a fisherman who played a key role in rescuing passengers from the wreck of the Brest. He is described as having strong arms and being fearless. His actions during the rescue and his physical characteristics, like the missing finger, are significant. He is also associated with the Lizard coast and the caves. His profession as a fisherman and his connection to the local community highlight his importance.</data>
