  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">A place in Cornwall, referenced as a destination for a walk. It is described as a location where the young folks went for a scramble, indicating it is a scenic or rugged area.&lt;SEP&gt;Penolver is a headland that rises in the sunshine, described as part of the scenic landscape near the Lizard. It is mentioned in the context of the group's walk and is associated with the natural beauty of the area. Penolver is a notable geographical feature in the region.&lt;SEP&gt;The Penolver is a location mentioned in the text, where the young folks go for a scramble. It is a geographical feature that adds to the setting of the narrative. While not as central as other locations, it contributes to the overall atmosphere and activities of the characters.</data>
