  <data key="d2">A location mentioned by the local man, which he claims to have lived in for 37 years. It is a significant part of his identity and daily life.&lt;SEP&gt;A town in Cornwall with a distinct character, described as having dark, narrow streets and a fish-like smell. It is mentioned as a place where the travelers seek directions to the sea and encounter a local resident who provides information about the pilchard fishery.&lt;SEP&gt;A town in Cornwall, England, known for its pilchard fishery and historical significance. It is the setting of the interaction between the narrator and the local man. The town is portrayed as a small but important place to its inhabitants.</data>
