<node id="SENNEN">
  <data key="d0">SENNEN</data>
  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">A small village near the Land's End, known for its fishing community and local schools. It is mentioned in the context of the fisher wife and her children, highlighting the close-knit nature of the community. The village is connected to the broader region through its proximity to Penzance and the Land's End.&lt;SEP&gt;A village in Cornwall, mentioned as a possible destination for an afternoon church service. It is associated with the narrator's acquaintance's family, who had a long-deceased father who was a curate there. This indicates a historical and personal connection to the place.&lt;SEP&gt;Sennen is a small village mentioned in the text. It is described as having an ancient church and a new school house, suggesting it is a place with historical and educational significance. The village is noted for its pretty cottages and lodgings, making it a potential holiday resort for families.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ca4427317d91b282aad105e4c1fcb34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fb3571cbea81efe6dfda2aa2199fdbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5e39286406a99236327034e4840f578</data>
