<node id="MR. ----">
  <data key="d0">MR. ----</data>
  <data key="d1">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d2">A long-dead curate of St. Sennen, who was known for walking across from Sennen to the parson's house and taking children on rambles. He is remembered as a fine young fellow and an excellent clergyman. His legacy lives on through the memories of the parson and the current generation of visitors to Land's End.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b9294464d408e527bddad8101fcc42d3</data>
</node>
<node id="BULLOCK FALLING INTO THE POOL">
  <data key="d0">BULLOCK FALLING INTO THE POOL</data>
  <data key="d1">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d2">A historical event involving a bullock that fell into a pool below the rocks at Land's End. The bullock was believed to be drowned but was later found swimming unhurt. This event highlights the unpredictable nature of the sea and the dangers present at Land's End, adding to the site's reputation as a place of both beauty and peril.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b9294464d408e527bddad8101fcc42d3</data>
</node>
<node id="SHIPWRECK NEAR THE BRISONS">
  <data key="d0">SHIPWRECK NEAR THE BRISONS</data>
  <data key="d1">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d2">A historical event involving a ship that went to pieces near the Brisons, a rock formation in the sea. The captain and his wife were stranded on the rock for two days and nights before being rescued. This event underscores the risks of navigating the waters around Land's End and the resilience of those who face such challenges.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b9294464d408e527bddad8101fcc42d3</data>
</node>
