<node id="UTHER PENDRAGON">
  <data key="d0">UTHER PENDRAGON</data>
  <data key="d1">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d2">Uther Pendragon was the King of Britain who fell in love with Ygrayne, the wife of the Duke of Cornwall. He besieged them in their castles, killed her husband, and married her. His actions set the stage for the birth of Arthur, making him a central figure in the Arthurian legend. Uther Pendragon's role is crucial in the narrative as the father of King Arthur.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f311566cae6280b6a50b89cb64a60d83</data>
</node>
<node id="YGRAYNE">
  <data key="d0">YGRAYNE</data>
  <data key="d1">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d2">Ygrayne is a character from Arthurian legend, associated with the story of King Arthur and the castle at Tintagel. She is mentioned in the context of the legend where she is shut up in one of the castles, and her husband is slain. Her story contributes to the tragic and mythical elements of the Arthurian tales.&lt;SEP&gt;Ygrayne was the wife of the Duke of Cornwall and the woman Uther Pendragon fell in love with. She was the mother of Arthur, and her marriage to Uther led to the birth of the future king. Her role in the narrative is significant as she is directly involved in the events that lead to Arthur's birth and the subsequent rise of his kingdom.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f311566cae6280b6a50b89cb64a60d83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-296767ee0019736ba3b3907d25d663f6</data>
</node>
<node id="ARTHUR">
  <data key="d0">ARTHUR</data>
  <data key="d1">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d2">Arthur is a central figure in the Arthurian legends, known for his leadership and the mythic events surrounding his life. He is often associated with the sword Excalibur and the tragic end of his reign. His story is deeply embedded in Cornish folklore and is a key element of the region's cultural identity. Arthur is also linked to the legend of the castle at Tintagel, where he is said to have been born.&lt;SEP&gt;Arthur was the son of Uther Pendragon and Ygrayne, born under mysterious circumstances and raised by Sir Ector. He became the legendary King of Britain, known for instituting the Order of Knights of the Round Table. Arthur's story is central to the Arthurian legend, and his reign is marked by both triumph and tragedy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f311566cae6280b6a50b89cb64a60d83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-296767ee0019736ba3b3907d25d663f6</data>
  <data key="d4">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}]</data>
</node>
<node id="GUINEVERE">
  <data key="d0">GUINEVERE</data>
  <data key="d1">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d2">Guinevere was the daughter of King Leodegrance and the wife of King Arthur. Her affair with Sir Launcelot led to the downfall of Arthur's kingdom. Guinevere's role in the narrative is pivotal, as her actions contribute to the tragic end of Arthur's reign and the eventual fall of Camelot.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f311566cae6280b6a50b89cb64a60d83</data>
  <data key="d4">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}]</data>
</node>
<node id="MERLIN">
  <data key="d0">MERLIN</data>
  <data key="d1">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d2">Merlin is a legendary figure mentioned in the text, associated with the 'little naked child' who was 'dear to Heaven.' He is linked to the history of Tintagel and the magical elements of the site. His presence adds to the mystical and mythical atmosphere of the location.&lt;SEP&gt;Merlin was an enchanter who played a key role in the upbringing of Arthur. He advised Uther Pendragon and ensured that Arthur was raised in secret before being revealed as the rightful heir to the throne. Merlin's influence over Arthur's life and the events leading to his coronation makes him a critical figure in the Arthurian legend.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f598012485ed9effde140d4a561fd5da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f311566cae6280b6a50b89cb64a60d83</data>
  <data key="d4">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}]</data>
</node>
<node id="DOZMARE POOL">
  <data key="d0">DOZMARE POOL</data>
  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">Dozmare Pool is a lake in Cornwall, associated with the legend of King Arthur. It is said to be the place where Arthur was taken after his death, and it is connected to the myth of his disappearance. Dozmare Pool is a significant location in the Arthurian legend, representing the mystical and supernatural elements of the story.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f311566cae6280b6a50b89cb64a60d83</data>
  <data key="d4">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 29}]</data>
</node>
<node id="MORGANE LA FAYE">
  <data key="d0">MORGANE LA FAYE</data>
  <data key="d1">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d2">Morgane la Faye is a mythical figure in Arthurian legend, often portrayed as a sorceress and the sister of King Arthur. She plays a significant role in the stories involving Arthur's death and the mystical elements of the Arthurian world. Her presence adds to the supernatural and legendary aspects of the Cornish tales.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-296767ee0019736ba3b3907d25d663f6</data>
</node>
<node id="TINTAGEL CASTLE">
  <data key="d0">TINTAGEL CASTLE</data>
  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">Tintagel Castle is a historic site located in Cornwall, England, and is closely associated with the legend of King Arthur. It is believed to be the birthplace of Arthur and is steeped in myth and history. The castle is a prominent location in the narrative, symbolizing the connection between the past and the present in Cornish culture.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-296767ee0019736ba3b3907d25d663f6</data>
  <data key="d4">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}]</data>
</node>
<node id="DELABOLE QUARRIES">
  <data key="d0">DELABOLE QUARRIES</data>
  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">Delabole quarries are a significant location in Cornwall, known for their slate mining operations. They are described as an un-sentimental place, contrasting with the romanticized legends of the region. The quarries represent the industrial aspect of the area and are part of the landscape that travelers encounter during their journey.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-296767ee0019736ba3b3907d25d663f6</data>
</node>
<node id="KING UTHER PENDRAGON">
  <data key="d0">KING UTHER PENDRAGON</data>
  <data key="d1">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d2">King Uther Pendragon is a key figure in Arthurian legend, known as the father of King Arthur. He is involved in the story of Ygrayne and is associated with the events at Tintagel Castle. His role in the legend highlights the complex relationships and conflicts within the Arthurian world.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-296767ee0019736ba3b3907d25d663f6</data>
</node>
<node id="TRISTRAM">
  <data key="d0">TRISTRAM</data>
  <data key="d1">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d2">Tristram is a knight from Arthurian legend, known for his love story with Iseult. He is mentioned in the narrative as part of the broader Arthurian tradition, highlighting the themes of love, betrayal, and tragedy that are common in these tales. His story is connected to the location of Tintagel and the broader Cornish mythology.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-296767ee0019736ba3b3907d25d663f6</data>
</node>
<node id="ISEULT">
  <data key="d0">ISEULT</data>
  <data key="d1">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d2">A woman known as 'Iseult of the white hands' who is mentioned as the second wife of the man described in the text. She is portrayed as innocent, simple, and dignified, and her relationship with the man is central to the narrative. Her significance lies in her role as a symbol of purity and the contrast to the more passionate and tragic characters in the Arthurian legends.&lt;SEP&gt;Iseult is a central character in the legend of Tristram and Iseult, known for her tragic love story with Tristram. She is mentioned in the narrative as part of the Arthurian tradition, emphasizing the emotional and dramatic elements of the tales. Her story is intertwined with the themes of love and fate that are prevalent in the Arthurian legends.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68ddd89fc902a4696967a79c5aea8055&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-296767ee0019736ba3b3907d25d663f6</data>
</node>
<node id="KING MARK">
  <data key="d0">KING MARK</data>
  <data key="d1">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d2">King Mark is a character from the Arthurian legend, associated with the story of Tristram and Iseult. He is mentioned in the narrative as the king who sends Tristram to fetch Iseult for his queen. His role in the legend highlights the political and personal conflicts that arise from the love story between Tristram and Iseult.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-296767ee0019736ba3b3907d25d663f6</data>
</node>
<node id="HE">
  <data key="d0">HE</data>
  <data key="d1">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d2">A person who is described as having married another Iseult and lived peacefully until his death. He is associated with the Arthurian legends and is linked to the theme of love and loss. His role in the narrative is central to the emotional core of the story. He is not explicitly named, but his actions and relationships are significant.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68ddd89fc902a4696967a79c5aea8055</data>
</node>
<node id="BOSSINNEY COVE">
  <data key="d0">BOSSINNEY COVE</data>
  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">A cove in the UK where the group of travelers visited. It is described as a picturesque location with a rocky path and a secluded beach. The cove is notable for its natural beauty and the presence of an old man and his donkeys, which adds to the narrative's reflective tone.</data>
