<node id="FERRABURY CHURCH">
  <data key="d0">FERRABURY CHURCH</data>
  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">Ferrabury Church is a historical site with a silent tower, mentioned in the text. It is connected to the story of the lost bells and the tragic shipwreck. The church's tower is described as mute, but it is still associated with the haunting sound of the lost bells during winter nights. This makes it an important cultural and historical landmark.</data>
