<node id="TREVELYANS">
  <data key="d3">chunk-369d72e297f786886a6ee02d55512e06</data>
  <data key="d2">The legend of the Trevelyans is closely tied to the rock of Goldsithney. According to the story, an ancestor of the Trevelyans saved himself by swimming his horse to safety when the fair land of Lyonesse was engulfed by the sea. This relationship highlights the historical and mythological significance of the rock and its connection to the Trevelyans.</data>
  <data key="d1">"UNKNOWN"</data>
