  <data key="d8">2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="WE" target="OUR LANDLADY">
  <data key="d5">0.8</data>
  <data key="d6">The relationship between the travelers and their landlady involves an exchange of decorative items. The travelers requested to remove certain ornamental items from their room, and in return, they were allowed to replace them with jars, salt-jars, or jam-pots for arranging wild flowers. This relationship reflects a mutual understanding and compromise between the two parties.</data>
  <data key="d7">chunk-12e1d0ddbd52f7c9b5db9fe78dbfee83</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="WE" target="THE GARDEN">
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
  <data key="d6">The relationship between the travelers and the garden involves a transformation of their living space. After removing the ornamental items, the travelers decorated their room with wild flowers, which created a more pleasant and natural atmosphere. This relationship highlights the impact of the garden on the travelers' experience and their ability to create a comfortable living environment.</data>
  <data key="d7">chunk-12e1d0ddbd52f7c9b5db9fe78dbfee83</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="WE" target="CORNISH COAST">
  <data key="d5">0.7</data>
  <data key="d6">The relationship between the travelers and the Cornish coast involves a deep appreciation for its natural beauty. The travelers describe the region as not picturesque but filled with a sense of freedom and joy. This relationship reflects the emotional and aesthetic connection between the travelers and the landscape.</data>
