  <data key="d5">1.2</data>
  <data key="d6">The 'young heads' have a direct relationship with the 'cringo,' as they are part of the local flora and are mentioned in the context of the group's collection efforts. This relationship reflects their interest in the natural environment and their efforts to gather and preserve these plants. The cringo is a notable feature of the Cornish coast and contributes to its unique character.</data>
