<edge source="LANDEWEDNACK" target="LANDEWEDNACK CHURCH">
  <data key="d5">0.9</data>
  <data key="d6">The relationship between Landewednack Church and the parish of Landewednack is direct and fundamental. The church is located within the parish and serves as a central religious and historical landmark. Its significance is tied to the community and the cultural identity of the area.</data>
  <data key="d7">chunk-a5dd17ac6c7028198a21adf7ff042f8e</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="LANDEWEDNACK CHURCH" target="CONGREGATION">
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
  <data key="d6">The relationship between the congregation and Landewednack Church is direct and spiritual. The congregation attends the church for worship, and their behavior during the service reflects their reverence and respect for the place. This relationship highlights the role of the church in the daily lives of the locals.</data>
  <data key="d7">chunk-a5dd17ac6c7028198a21adf7ff042f8e</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="LANDEWEDNACK CHURCH" target="CORNISH LANGUAGE">
  <data key="d5">0.8</data>
  <data key="d6">The relationship between the Cornish language and Landewednack Church is historical and cultural. The last sermon in Cornish was preached in the church in 1678, marking the end of the language's use in religious contexts. This relationship underscores the linguistic and cultural transformation of the region.</data>
  <data key="d7">chunk-a5dd17ac6c7028198a21adf7ff042f8e</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="LANDEWEDNACK CHURCH" target="PLAGUE IN 1645">
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
  <data key="d6">The relationship between the plague in 1645 and the churchyard of Landewednack is historical and commemorative. The victims of the plague are buried in a specific section of the churchyard, and their resting place remains undisturbed. This relationship reflects the church's role in preserving the memory of past tragedies.</data>
  <data key="d7">chunk-a5dd17ac6c7028198a21adf7ff042f8e</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="BLACK DOG" target="CONGREGATION">
