</edge>
<edge source="YOUNG MOTHER" target="YOUNG CORNISHMAN">
  <data key="d5">1.6</data>
  <data key="d6">The young Cornishman's actions have an indirect effect on the adults around him, influencing their interactions and responses. This second-order relationship highlights the impact of a child's behavior on the broader social environment. The adults' reactions to the child's mischief reflect their roles and responsibilities.&lt;SEP&gt;The young mother has a close relationship with her child, expressing both pride and concern for his behavior. This relationship is direct and reflects the emotional and practical aspects of parenthood. The mother's dialogue and actions demonstrate her deep connection to her child and her efforts to manage his energy and mischief.</data>
