<edge source="THE SEA" target="THE MERMAIDS">
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
  <data key="d6">The relationship between the sea and the characters is one of attraction and temptation. The sea's gentle waves invite the characters to swim, creating a sense of adventure and connection with nature. This relationship highlights the beauty and power of the natural world and its influence on human behavior and emotions. The sea's presence shapes the characters' activities and contributes to their sense of joy and wonder.</data>
  <data key="d7">chunk-0c276072b502ce264a92ee400fbb2def</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="THE SEA" target="THE CHARACTERS">
  <data key="d5">0.7</data>
  <data key="d6">The relationship between the characters and the natural elements, such as the sea and the sky, is one of immersion and reflection. The characters are deeply connected to their environment, finding joy and inspiration in the beauty of nature. This relationship influences their emotional state and contributes to their sense of contentment and peace. It also reflects the broader theme of harmony between humans and the natural world.</data>
  <data key="d7">chunk-0c276072b502ce264a92ee400fbb2def</data>
  <data key="d8">2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="SAND-CASTLES" target="THE WAVES">
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
  <data key="d6">The relationship between the sand-castles and the waves is one of destruction and impermanence. The waves ultimately sweep away the sand-castles, symbolizing the transient nature of human creations and the power of natural forces. This relationship reflects the theme of impermanence and the inevitability of change. It also highlights the contrast between human efforts and the enduring power of nature.</data>
  <data key="d7">chunk-0c276072b502ce264a92ee400fbb2def</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="SAND-CASTLES" target="THE CHARACTERS">
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
  <data key="d6">The relationship between the characters and the sand-castles is one of creation and attachment. The characters build the sand-castles as a form of play and creativity, forming a bond with their temporary structures. This relationship highlights the human desire for expression and the emotional significance of even fleeting creations. It also underscores the theme of impermanence and the acceptance of change.</data>
  <data key="d7">chunk-0c276072b502ce264a92ee400fbb2def</data>
  <data key="d8">2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="RECTOR" target="COMMUNITY">
  <data key="d5">0.9</data>
  <data key="d6">The rectory tea served as a direct link between the rector and the broader community, including both the wealthy and the humble. The event facilitated interactions among different social groups, reinforcing the rector's role as a unifying figure. This relationship highlights the importance of the tea as a social and cultural event.</data>
  <data key="d7">chunk-5e302b5e22b09ab16666a0e39faaadeb</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="RECTORY TEA" target="CHURCH SERVICE">
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
  <data key="d6">The church service had a second-order relationship with the rectory tea, as it was a follow-up event that brought together many of the same attendees. The service reinforced the spiritual and communal aspects of the tea, creating a deeper sense of unity among participants. This relationship shows how events can build upon one another to strengthen community bonds.</data>
  <data key="d7">chunk-5e302b5e22b09ab16666a0e39faaadeb</data>
  <data key="d8">2</data>
</edge>
