  <data key="d8">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="JOHN" target="WRECK OF THE BREST">
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
  <data key="d6">John had a direct relationship with the wreck of the Brest, as he was involved in rescuing passengers from it. His actions during the rescue demonstrated his bravery and commitment to saving lives. This relationship highlights his role as a fisherman and his connection to the coastal community.</data>
  <data key="d7">chunk-9b862cd9f3d4a2a5394fa477c897d562</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="JOHN" target="LIZARD COAST">
  <data key="d5">0.8</data>
  <data key="d6">John had a direct relationship with the Lizard coast, as he lived and worked there. He was familiar with the area and used his knowledge to navigate the waters and assist in rescues. This relationship emphasizes his connection to the local environment and his role as a fisherman.</data>
  <data key="d7">chunk-9b862cd9f3d4a2a5394fa477c897d562</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="BELLOWS" target="LADIES">
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
  <data key="d6">The relationship between the ladies and the natural features of Kynance Cove, such as the Bellows and Asparagus Island, evolves as they engage in activities like climbing and observing the environment. This relationship is influenced by their adventurous spirit and the challenges they face in the natural landscape.</data>
